    "final_text": "The audit found two real problems in my first fix, and both are now fixed. All 24 tests pass on the final code, and the completion receipt is written.\n\n**What the audit fixed:**\n- **100% discount:** `total - total * discount / 100` left tiny rounding errors. A 100% discount on 0.07 \u00d7 3 returned -2.78e-17 instead of 0, and 1 of 200,000 random carts got a negative total at a valid discount. `getTotal` now computes `total * (1 - discount / 100)`, which gives exactly 0 at 100% off and never goes below zero. In the same random test there were no bad results.\n- **Error messages:** the helper that formats error messages crashed on an unusual kind of object (one with no prototype), so the useful message was lost. It now uses Node's `util.inspect`. As a side effect, strings in error messages now show single quotes (`'pear'`) instead of double quotes.\n- **Tests:** loops that check several bad inputs now name the input that got through when one fails. The invalid-discount test now checks the result through `getTotal()` instead of reading the cart's internal `discount` field.\n\nEach of the original 5 bugs is still caught by its own test when put back alone, and so is the old discount formula.\n\n**Not done:**\n- **The review step:** Dex's `/dxreview` step didn't have its usual setup, so I ran the review in this session and reported it here instead of publishing a review receipt.\n- **Edge cases left unchanged:**\n  - Re-adding an item at a different price keeps the first price, as the original code did.\n  - Extremely large quantities or prices pass validation and can overflow.\n  - Totals aren't rounded, because the number of decimal places depends on the currency.\n  - `items` and `discount` are plain fields a caller can change directly, which skips validation. That's how the original class was written.\n\nThere are three commits on `fix/cart-bugs`, not pushed because the repo has no remote.\n\nPROMPT_COMPLETE",
